[ti:2-09-创新]
[00:00.00]The cartoon depicts that a strong person is trying to dig gold out of a huge stone.
[00:06.69]Holding an ax with his firm hands,
[00:09.49]he is hewing out of the stone of despair a piece of precious gold.
[00:14.78]The caption indicates that,
[00:17.18]“Only through innovation can we make progress,
[00:21.17]while sticking to old ways means regression.” The purpose of the drawing is to show us that utmost importance should be attached to innovation and creativity.
[00:34.46]To begin with,
[00:35.66]the spirit of innovation could be said to be the watchword or motto of science.
[00:42.15]Think about the innumerable times a scientific experiment must be carried out,
[00:48.84]all the laboratory tests,
[00:51.04]all the live trials,
[00:52.74]before a new medicine or vaccine is discovered.
[00:56.73]In addition,
[00:57.83]many of today’s business successes can be attributed to innovation.
[01:03.63]For instance,
[01:04.83]I personally worked in such a company.
[01:08.02]It was only after four years and four tries of different business models that its entrepreneur finally succeeded,
[01:17.61]and became the chairman of one of the largest Internet companies.
[01:23.11]To sum up,
[01:23.90]in any field of endeavour,
[01:26.10]whether it be in medicine,
[01:28.30]engineering or in business,
[01:30.70]it seems necessary to put great emphasis on innovation before one can finally achieve success.
